            <ArticleTitle>[Left ventricular thrombosis with acute myocardial infarction: morphologic aspects indicative of an elevated embolic risk].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this study the authors evaluate the potentiality of two-dimensional echocardiography to detect the left ventricular thrombus in the myocardial infarction. The authors emphasize the morphological echocardiographic patterns suggestive of the high embolic risk of the ventricular thrombus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
